From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: msm_geni_serial: force the HS UART qup05 mux on open

On monaco/dace the only place that muxes the HS UART pins (GPIO 26-29:
TX/RX/CTS/RTS) to the qup05 function is
msm_geni_serial_resources_on() -> pinctrl_select_state(geni_gpio_active), and
that is only called from the runtime-PM cycle (runtime_resume) and from
msm_geni_console_setup (console). The HS UART open
(msm_geni_serial_startup) does NOT call it, so the device's pinctrl state stays
at "shutdown" (gpio function) and the UART block neither receives nor sends
anything: the WCN3988 BT looks mute even though the vendor HAL does the whole
bring-up (PowerUpChip, wakeup, bauds, Get Version) and the SE is clean
(rx_fifo_sts:0x0, geni_ios:0x0).

Verified live with /sys/kernel/debug/pinctrl/pinctrl-handles:
  device: 4a94000.qcom,qup_uart current state: shutdown
    state: active ... function: qup05 (179)
(the active state exists and is correct, but it is not selected).

The DT is identical to aurora's (Pixel Watch 2, same SW5100 and same kernel).
A pinctrl "hog" on the controller DOES mux but claims the pins and breaks the
UART probe (msm_geni_serial loads with 0 ports). That is why we force the mux
here, when opening the UART, with the return value visible.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]

Signed-off-by: dace bring-up <dace@localhost>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c
@@ -3654,6 +3654,21 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * dace: on this device the runtime-PM cycle does not run, so the
+	 * pinctrl_select_state(active) from resources_on() (the only place that
+	 * muxes the HS UART pins to qup05) never executes: pins 26-29 stay at
+	 * function=gpio and the WCN3988 BT looks mute. The mux is forced here,
+	 * when opening the UART.
+	 */
+	if (likely(!uart_console(uport))) {
+		ret = pinctrl_select_state(msm_port->serial_rsc.geni_pinctrl,
+					   msm_port->serial_rsc.geni_gpio_active);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err(uport->dev, "%s: failed to select active pinctrl: %d\n",
+				__func__, ret);
+	}
+
 	get_tx_fifo_size(msm_port);
 	if (!msm_port->port_setup) {
 		ret = msm_geni_serial_port_setup(uport);
